package agent

const goalContractGuidance = `
Save goal_type for new goals: inspection means completing a check of the scope the user specified and can be satisfied by evidenced negative coverage; outcome means obtaining an actual result and requires result evidence. required_checks lists the required objects/mechanisms/quantities item by item. When the user only asks for a best-effort exploration, write it as an inspection with an explicit scope and budget; don't invent an outcome that requires finding a vulnerability/flag. A result the user explicitly asks to obtain cannot be downgraded to a check. The earlier "never make check steps into goals" only forbids inventing steps yourself; checks the user explicitly asks to complete must be saved as inspection with required_checks.`

const checkWorkflowGuidance = `
For every required check, provide check={target: the normalized actual target/endpoint, mechanism: the check mechanism} in add_intent. This identity doesn't change with summary, Worker or rebuilt work. Recovery uses retry_of and recovery_change, explaining the previous obstacle and the condition changed this time; the same check at most three times, and changing identity to evade the limit is not allowed.
The Worker saves result=positive/negative/partial/blocked, scope, evidence, gaps, and barrier/next_action with record_fact.checkpoint. A negative result covers only the scope actually completed; interruptions, errors and exhausted budget can only be recorded as partial/blocked. Keep observed facts and inferred conclusions separate; an inference alone cannot support a goal being met.
For authentication checks, checkpoint.auth saves the real request specification, the authorized attempt budget and the list of fixed candidate references (opaque IDs, no passwords); each item's state remaining/failed/skipped/verified, plus the number of requests actually sent, attempts (errors/rate limiting also consume the original budget). Save immediately after executing; before resuming read the original checkpoint and run remaining candidates only while the original budget still allows. Stop on lockout/rate limiting/CAPTCHA and record why; don't expand the authorized candidates or budget. Verify a low-impact read after authentication and the real identity's privileges, and hand identity/identity_evidence over to identity-dependent work; HTTP 200, a Cookie or a redirect alone doesn't prove success. Misses in a small scope don't rule out the whole authentication direction.
The Planner reads the actual checkpoints and incomplete items before deciding to prove the goal or recover. When recovery is impossible, keep the gaps; repeated runs without new evidence don't count as progress. When the system has made no effective progress for three consecutive rounds with no work in flight, it pauses this run for review; the goal stays open and must not be falsely marked met.`
